# The client inputs are kept byte for byte as received: each manifest records the
# SHA-256 of the file as MAIIC sent it, and the landing gates refuse a file whose
# hash differs. The repository's "* text=auto" would store these files with LF and
# hand them back with CRLF only where core.autocrlf is true, so a clone on a Linux
# server (or with autocrlf off) would get other bytes and every pack would be
# quarantined. No line-ending conversion here, in either direction (14 October 2026).
*.csv -text
*.json -text
*.sql -text
